# PassTheStick — Project context

## What this project is

**PassTheStick** is a Windows desktop utility that lets a group of friends take turns controlling a single-player game on one person's PC. Everyone is already watching the host's screen via Discord screenshare. PassTheStick handles only one thing: whose keyboard (or controller) is currently active.

- The **host** runs the game and the PassTheStick host app.
- **Guests** run a tiny PassTheStick client app, enter a 4-character room code, and wait for the stick.
- The **host passes the stick** via a hotkey or tray UI. Whoever has the stick has live keyboard/controller input into the game. Everyone else is blocked.
- A **relay server** (Node.js WebSocket, deployed free on Fly.io) routes messages between clients. It never touches game state — it is only a message broker.

There is no screen capture, no video stream, no voice chat. Discord handles all of that. PassTheStick is a pure input routing tool.

---

## Technology decisions (do not change without strong reason)

| Layer | Choice | Reason |
|-------|--------|--------|
| Host + Guest app | C# .NET 8, Windows-only | Best Win32 P/Invoke, WPF transparent overlay, strong NuGet ecosystem |
| Keyboard hook | `SetWindowsHookEx(WH_KEYBOARD_LL)` via P/Invoke | System-wide hook, fires before game processes input, works with DirectInput + RawInput |
| Keyboard injection | `SendInput()` with `KEYEVENTF_SCANCODE` | Goes through hardware input model — required for modern games using Raw Input or DirectInput. Never use PostMessage or VK-only SendInput. |
| Controller read (guest) | `SharpDX.XInput` or `SDL2-CS` | Reads any XInput-compatible controller on guest PC |
| Controller injection (host) | `ViGEmBus` + `Nefarius.ViGEm.Client` NuGet | Industry-standard virtual Xbox controller driver. DS4Windows ships this to millions. |
| Double-input prevention | `HidHide` (bundled in installer, configured programmatically) | Hides physical controller from game, only virtual ViGEm controller is visible |
| Network transport | `System.Net.WebSockets` (client) + `ws` npm package (server) | Low overhead, works through firewalls/NAT, no polling |
| Relay server | Node.js, ~80 lines, zero dependencies beyond `ws` | Deploys free on Fly.io, stateless, rooms live only in memory |
| Overlay UI | WPF transparent window (`AllowsTransparency=true`, `Topmost=true`, `WindowStyle=None`) | Native, always-on-top, compatible with windowed and borderless games |
| Installer | Inno Setup | Free, handles optional ViGEmBus + HidHide driver components, UAC elevation |
| License | MIT (open source, free) | Maximum reach and trust. No license keys. No paywalls. |

