## WebSocket message protocol

All messages are JSON. Keep payloads minimal — keyboard events should be ~40 bytes.

- **JOIN** — Guest → Relay: `{ type:"JOIN", roomCode:"WOLF", name:"jakub" }`
- **PLAYER_LIST** — Relay → Host: `{ type:"PLAYER_LIST", players:[{id, name, connected}] }`
- **PASS_STICK** — Host → Relay → All: `{ type:"PASS_STICK", toId:"abc123" }`
- **YOU_HAVE_IT** — Relay → Guest: `{ type:"YOU_HAVE_IT" }`
- **KEY_EVENT** — ActiveGuest → Relay → Host: `{ type:"KEY_EVENT", vk:87, sc:17, down:true }` (guest sends both vk and sc; host uses MapVirtualKey(vk, MAPVK_VK_TO_VSC) for host layout)
- **PAD_STATE** — ActiveGuest → Relay → Host: `{ type:"PAD_STATE", btns:4096, lx:0, ly:0, rx:0, ry:0, lt:0, rt:200 }` (send only when state differs from previous frame)
- **PING** / **PONG** — Both: `{ type:"PING", ts:1710000000000 }` / `{ type:"PONG", ts:1710000000000 }`

Relay forwards KEY_EVENT and PAD_STATE only to the host in the same room. It never broadcasts input events to other guests — only control messages (PLAYER_LIST, PASS_STICK, YOU_HAVE_IT) are broadcast. Room expiry: 30-minute idle timeout per room (reset on any message).

